<title>POLAND: Polish bond auction schedule for Q1 1997.</title>
<headline>Polish bond auction schedule for Q1 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish finance ministry has released the following bond auction schedule for the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>NOTE. In the bond symbol in brackets the first two letters denote the type of bond, the following two digits are the month of maturity and the last two digits the year of maturity of the particular issue. The amount of bonds on offer is announced a week before the tender.</p>
<p> DATE		   BOND TYPE			     BOND SYMBOL</p>
<p> Jan 14	   - floating 10-yr bond tender	     (DZ0107)</p>
<p> Jan 16	   - fixed 2-yr, 5-yr bond tender  (OS0299,OS0202)</p>
<p> Jan 20-Feb 2   - index-linked 1-yr bond subscription  (IR0398)</p>
<p> Jan 21	   - floating three-year bond tender	(TZ0200)</p>
<p> Jan 28	   - index-linked 1-yr bond tender	 *(RP0398)</p>
<p> Feb 3-April 30 - floating 3-yr bond public sale	 (TZ0200)</p>
<p> Feb 20	   - fixed 5-yr bond tender (assimilated) (OS0601)</p>
<p> Feb 25	   - index-linked 1-yr bond tender	 *(RP0398)</p>
<p> March 3-May 28 - index-linked 1-yr bond public sale   (IR0398)</p>
<p> March 11	 - floating 10-yr bond tender    (DZ0406,DZ0407)</p>
<p> March 20	 - fixed 5-yr bond tender (assimilated) (OS0601)</p>
<p>* Index-linked one-year bond issues of the IR series are for the public and carry interest of 300 basis points above year-on-year inflation two months before maturity. The RP series of the one-year bonds is sold at primary tenders for institutions and does not have the 300 bp margin above inflation in its interest mechanism.</p>
<p>The five-year assimilated bonds and the DZ0406 10-year bond are from unsold 1996 issues.</p>
<p>-- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
